# Private material — deliberately kept out of this repo because it is public.
# These files still live in the working directory; they are just not tracked.
#   - personal photographs, not corporate artwork
#   - internal strategy notes
Images/Hari.png
Images/logo 2.png
website content.docx
~$*.docx

# CVs and résumés — these carry home addresses, personal phone numbers and
# private email. Source material only; never publish. Processed headshots that
# belong on the site live in public/brand/team/ instead.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to the repository root. Without it, and because
# Windows sets core.ignorecase=true, the pattern also swallowed
# public/brand/team/ and silently kept every headshot out of the repo.
/Team/
*.pdf
*.docx

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

# Throwaway face-framing previews (scripts/face-grid-preview.mjs)
.tmp-face/

# Full-resolution headshot sources. Same rule as /Team/ — only the cropped
# 800px webp in public/brand/team belongs in a public repo.
Images/Team members/

# Social posting drafts — held back while this repository is public.
#
# The queue is not secret in the sense of containing a credential; it holds no
# token and never will. It is simply the marketing calendar, and a public repo
# would publish every unapproved draft and the posting schedule with it.
#
# The scheduled workflow reads social/queue.json from the repository, so the
# automation stays inactive until these are committed. Make the repository
# private (Settings -> General -> Danger Zone -> Change visibility), then
# remove these two lines and commit the queue to switch it on.
social/queue.json
social/CALENDAR.md
social/original.json
